We need to extend the existing Local Agent to support API execution for API Studio.

This should reuse the current architecture (agent + backend + WebSocket + sessionId). Do NOT create a separate system.

---

## ARCHITECTURE

* API requests should execute on user machine via Local Agent
* Backend continues orchestration
* Frontend UI remains same (Postman-like interface)

---

1. NEW COMMAND TYPE

---

Backend should send a new command to agent:

{
"type": "API_REQUEST",
"sessionId": "<id>",
"method": "GET/POST/PUT/DELETE",
"url": "<full_url>",
"headers": { ... },
"body": "<raw/json/form-data>",
"timeout": <ms>
}

---

2. AGENT IMPLEMENTATION

---

Agent should:

1. Receive API_REQUEST via WebSocket

2. Execute request locally using:

   * Python: httpx (preferred) or requests

3. Support:

   * HTTP methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH
   * Headers
   * JSON body
   * form-data (basic support)
   * query params (via URL)

4. Handle HTTPS (certs automatically available via OS)

5. Capture:

   * status code
   * response headers
   * response body
   * response time

---

3. RESPONSE FORMAT

---

Agent sends back:

{
"type": "API_RESPONSE",
"sessionId": "<id>",
"status": 200,
"headers": { ... },
"body": "<response_body>",
"duration": <ms>,
"error": null
}

If error:

{
"type": "API_RESPONSE",
"sessionId": "<id>",
"error": "<error_message>"
}

---

4. BACKEND CHANGES

---

* Route API requests to agent using sessionId mapping
* Do NOT execute API on server if agent is connected
* Forward response to frontend

---

5. FRONTEND BEHAVIOR

---

* Keep UI unchanged (Postman-style)

* On "Send" button:

  * trigger backend API execution
  * backend routes to agent

* Display:

  * response body
  * status code
  * headers
  * response time

* Show message:
  "Request executed locally on your machine"

---

6. AGENT DETECTION

---

Before API execution:

* Ensure agent is running (reuse existing /health check)
* If not:
  show "Agent required" modal (reuse existing flow)

---

7. SECURITY

---

* Do NOT log sensitive headers (Authorization, tokens)
* Do NOT persist request/response unless required
* Keep execution in-memory

---

8. TIMEOUT & ERROR HANDLING

---

* Respect timeout from request

* Handle:

  * connection errors
  * DNS errors
  * SSL errors
  * timeouts

* Return clean error message to frontend

---

9. NON-GOALS

---

* Do NOT add new UI complexity
* Do NOT move API execution to server for cert-based APIs
* Do NOT duplicate agent logic

---

## GOAL

Enable API Studio to execute requests locally via agent, ensuring support for:

* certificate-based APIs
* VPN/internal APIs
* restricted enterprise environments

Keep implementation simple, reusable, and aligned with existing agent architecture.
